>>What is Hibernate?

>Hibernate is a Java ORM (Object-Relational Mapping) framework that helps us interact with a database using Java objects instead of writing SQL queries manually.
@Entity
public class Student {

    @Id
    private int id;

    private String name;
    private String email;
}

answer Student
-----------------
id
name
email

INSERT INTO student VALUES (1, 'Amit', 'amit@gmail.com');

Why do we use Hibernate?
Reduces the amount of SQL code
Maps Java classes → database tables
Maps Java objects → table records
Handles CRUD operations
Supports relationships like OneToOne, OneToMany, ManyToOne
Provides transaction management and caching features
.................................
Hibernate vs JPA

This is important for interviews:

JPA is a specification, while Hibernate is an implementation of JPA.

For example, in Spring Boot we commonly use:

Spring Boot
     ↓
Spring Data JPA
     ↓
Hibernate
     ↓
MySQL

